2. Load Data 

Read Survey Files: 

 Read survey data from J:/, L:/, and the re_extract folder. 

Exclude VR and Vital information data, subset to survey providers that we know have GPS information. 

The re_extract folder was created when NCH team identified there were older surveys that needed to be re-extracted, 65 NIDS. 2 were dropped due to Winnower breaking, and empty rows in Winnmiill. 

Combine all three data objects. 

  

Quality Checks 

Make sure all NIDS from the re-extracted folder have made it into the pre-processed dataset before moving on. Re-extraction may be needed. 

 Check that expected NIDs from LBWSG codebook are included. 

Report any missing NIDs, which may require re-extraction. 

 

Hot Fixes: 

 Adjust specific NIDs for Peru surveys to match year-specific GPS data.(Parent to child NIDS) 

  

4. Geocodebook 

  

Load MBG geocodebook data (geo_mbg). 

Optionally load SAE data, but prefer MBG if point data exists or has appropriate admin-level matches. 

As a quick alternative to get around geocodebook function error happening, MBG data was downloaded from Geocodebook Database. Then, to make sure we weren't missing at lat/long from SAE – the final missing nids(bottom of script) were checked in the geocodebook database to identify missing lat/longs. None were found, SAE had shapefile information for those NIDS. 

  

Remove geocodebook entries without valid geographic info. 

   

5. Data Merge 

 

Convert NIDs to character for consistency. 

Merge survey data (compiled_dt) with geography data (sae_mbg_bind) on NID, country code, and geospatial ID. 

Clean and rename columns for clarity. 

  

6. Special Handling for Missing GPS: 

These surveys have GPS information, but that data is currently missing in database. So the temp. fix is to add them here: 

 Tanzania (538795)  - missing GPS in database, merged to GPS file 

 Bangladesh (527880) - missing GPS in database, merged to GPS file 

Then, remove duplicate NIDs from main dataset before adding corrected rows. 

  

7. Final Dataset Assembly and Filtering 

 

Combine all data into final, ensuring uniqueness. 

Missing Latitude/Longitude: 

Summarize missingness by NID 

Go to GHDX Tools: https://internal-ghdx.healthdata.org/records-files-by-nid/ to identify surveys where there could be GPS data 

 Remove surveys where lat/long is 100% missing.  

 

Quality Checks: 

Identify new and dropped NIDs compared to previous dataset. 

Output summary table of surveys. 

  

Output 

  Save the final dataset as a .parquet file   

  

Notes & Limitations 

Excludes VR surveys due to missing geographic info. 

Hot fixes are applied for specific NIDs (Peru, Tanzania, Bangladesh) to align data by year or correct GPS info. 

Assumes access to external tools like geocodebook databases and GHDX Record + NID Tool for further missing data checks. 

Commented code for SAE/MBG preference logic is left for future refinement. 

Certain file paths and filenames must be filled in by the user. 